Hi folks,

I've just made a change to the identify scroll/spell feature to
make it easier to select the items you want to identify.

For instance, if you have two wands with inventory letters a and b, 
and you really want to identify b, but might also like to identify a,
it is currently not possible to first identify b, then (if you can
identify more items) identify a.

This change allow you to identify a set of items, and then if you
can identify more items, specify a new set of items and identify
them.  Also, if the spell lets you identify everything, then 
this happens automatically.

Search for 'case SCR_IDENTIFY' in read.c, and modify it as follows:

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
        case SCR_IDENTIFY:
                /* known = TRUE; */
                if(confused)
                        You("identify this as an identify scroll.");
                else
                        pline("This is an identify scroll.");
                if (sobj->blessed || (!sobj->cursed && !rn2(5)))
                        cval = rn2(5);
                        /* Note: if rn2(5)==0, identify all items */
                else    cval = 1;
                useup(sobj);
                makeknown(SCR_IDENTIFY);
#ifdef SPELLS
        id:
#endif
                if(!confused)
#ifdef SNELLING_MODS /* Enhanced Identify */
                {
                        if (invent && (cval == 0)) {
                                pline("Identifying all items.");
                                (void) askchain(invent, TRUE, NULL, TRUE,
                                    identify, NULL, cval, "identify");
                        } else
                        while(invent && (cval > 0)) {
                                cval -= ggetobj("identify", identify, cval);
                                if (cval > 0) {
                                        pline("Identify more items? ");
                                        if (yn_function(ynchars, 'y')=='n') {
                                                cval=0;
                                        }
                                }
                        }
                }
#else /* SNELLING_MODS Enhanced Identify */
                    while(invent && !ggetobj("identify", identify, cval));
#endif /* SNELLING_MODS Enhanced Identify */
                return(1);
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

You have to also define SNELLING_MODS for this to work properly as written
above.  (The reason I surround all my changes with "#ifdef SNELLING_MODS"
is to allow me to easily find all my changes.  It also lets me remove them
all by simply changing one line.)

